  "description": "Lawful Development Certificate for an existing front lightwell, comprising a recessed voidspace below street level at front of property",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span id=&quot;docs-internal-guid-1664b004-7fff-d758-1795-979997e07757&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p dir=&quot;ltr&quot; style=&quot;line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;margin-top:6pt;margin-bottom:6pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;&quot;&gt;The application is supported by substantial evidence demonstrating that the front lightwell at the property has been continuously in place for over four years, thereby meeting the requirements of Section 191 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 (as amended). Accordingly, the LPA is satisfied that on the balance of probability the development is lawful and should issue a certificate under Section 191 of the Act.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
